Package: backgammonr
Type: Package
Title: Thompson-Centered Finite-Budget Backgammon Rollout Allocation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "OpenAI",
           family = "Assistant",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "assistant@example.com")
Author: OpenAI Assistant [aut, cre]
Maintainer: OpenAI Assistant <assistant@example.com>
Description: Statistical-computing tools for finite-budget rollout allocation
    in backgammon, centered on Thompson sampling for best-action
    identification under simulation noise. The package combines a C++
    backgammon engine with Monte Carlo action-evaluation infrastructure,
    high-budget reference estimation, and baseline comparison methods
    (equal/UCB/OCBA/greedy). Outputs emphasize proxy probability of correct
    selection, simple regret, value-estimation error, and runtime
    speed-accuracy tradeoffs.
